{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevR5pfgZWXUSqXQrRNX8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a clear understanding of the codebase. Let me document the key findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order.kt:11 - Order data class (no status field yet)\n- OrderController.kt:22-42 - CREATE and GET endpoints with error handling\n- OrderRepository.kt:13-26 - In-memory ConcurrentHashMap storage\n- Shipment.kt:23-27 - ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController.kt:26-44 - Creates shipments with CREATED status\n- ShipmentRepository.kt:13-26 - In-memory storage (needs findByOrderId method)\n- ApiExceptions.kt:18-30 - ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- ApiError.kt:31-37 - ErrorCode enum\n- GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28 - Central exception handling\n\n**Conventions established:**\n- Exceptions map to HTTP status via ApiException\n- Error responses use ApiError envelope with code, message, fields\n- Tests verify both HTTP status AND response body (jsonPath)\n- Repositories use ConcurrentHashMap for in-memory storage\n- Tests reset state in @BeforeEach\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt - Add status field and enum\n2. OrderController.kt - Add cancel endpoint\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt - Add findByOrderId method\n4. ShipmentController.kt - Block shipment creation for cancelled orders\n5. ApiError.kt - Add error codes for new scenarios\n6. OrderControllerTest.kt - Add cancel endpoint tests\n\n**Risks:**\n- Race conditions between checking order state and updating shipments\n- Need atomicity: either all shipments cancel or none do\n- Must ensure proper error handling preserves order/shipment state on conflict\n\n**Open questions:** None - all cases are clearly specified.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class and create OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED).\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt**: No changes needed - existing save/findById work with new field.\n\n3. **OrderController.kt**: Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Throws 404 if order not found\n   - Returns success if already CANCELLED\n   - If ACTIVE and any shipment is CONFIRMED: throw 409, change nothing\n   - If ACTIVE: set to CANCELLED, cancel all CREATED shipments, return updated order\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method to query shipments by order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**: In create endpoint, check if order exists and is not CANCELLED; throw 409 if CANCELLED.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt**: Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code for shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancel active order with no shipments\n   - Cancel active order with created shipments\n   - Retry cancel on already cancelled order\n   - Reject cancel when shipment is confirmed\n   - Return 404 for unknown order\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using a separate CancelOrderService class: Too much abstraction for simple in-memory operations; the controller can orchestrate repository calls directly as it does for create.\n- Storing cancelled shipments as separate status instead of updating: Would require finding and updating shipments; current design is cleaner.\n- Adding a `cancelledAt` timestamp instead of status enum: The ticket explicitly asks for status field; timestamp would be extra complexity.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Via |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----|\n| Cancel unknown order | Order (not found) | None | 404 OrderNotFoundException | ResourceNotFoundException → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Cancel CANCELLED order | Order (found, CANCELLED) | None | 200 Order | Normal response |\n| Cancel ACTIVE, no shipments | Order (found, ACTIVE), Shipments (empty) | Order (CANCELLED) | 200 Order | Normal response |\n| Cancel ACTIVE, CREATED shipments | Order (found, ACTIVE), Shipments (found, CREATED) | Order (CANCELLED), Shipments (CANCELLED) | 200 Order | Normal response |\n| Cancel ACTIVE, has CONFIRMED shipment | Order (found, ACTIVE), Shipments (found, has CONFIRMED) | None | 409 ConflictException | ConflictException → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Create shipment on ACTIVE order | Order (found, ACTIVE), Shipment (not exists) | Shipment (CREATED) | 201 Shipment | Normal response |\n| Create shipment on CANCELLED order | Order (found, CANCELLED), Shipment (not exists) | None | 409 ConflictException | ConflictException → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Create shipment on unknown order | Order (not found), Shipment (not exists) | Shipment (CREATED) | 201 Shipment | Current behavior (no order existence check) |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. Test cancel active order succeeds and returns CANCELLED order\n2. Test cancel active order cancels CREATED shipments\n3. Test cancel CANCELLED order returns success with no state change\n4. Test cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment rejects with 409 and no state change\n5. Test cancel unknown order returns 404\n6. Test create shipment on CANCELLED order rejects with 409\n7. Test create shipment on ACTIVE order succeeds (existing behavior still works)\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1141,"cache_read_input_tokens":20491,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1141},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2196d852-8638-440f-8f77-1deb717b65e1","uuid":"73972c0d-7c6e-4b2f-b1fc-fc7978afafb1","timestamp":"2026-09-10T20:48:35.108Z","request_id":"req_011CevR5pBAVnaoqh8YrYRdm"}
